  "s_fields_written": [
    "no direct store to S appears in the helper body",
    "via the map insert call 0x474b620 on &S+0x20 (map words at S+0x20..0x40, including the bucket allocation)",
    "via recursion into child S values stored in map buckets (bucket+0x18), not into the 0x40 bytes of S itself"
  ],
  "phases": [
    "split: searcher for \"::\" over (key ptr, key len); tag 1 -> head = key[..idx], tail = key[idx+2..]; no match -> head = whole key, tail empty; char-boundary guards fail through the slice-error slot 0x64df670",
    "probe (only if S+0x38 != 0): FNV-1a head hash with 0xff terminator, top-7-bit control pattern, 16-byte control-group probe of the S+0x20/S+0x28 table; hit needs bucket+0x10 == head len and bcmp(bucket+0x08, head, len) == 0; an empty control byte (0xff) is a miss",
    "hit: recurse into bucket+0x18 child S with (tail ptr, tail len, copy of mapped block, flag byte, first word); return",
    "miss with tail: build child S {S+0x00, S+0x18, copied mapped array, S+0x18, static empty-map block}, recurse on the tail, then insert the head segment with that child as value",
    "leaf (empty tail): if flag byte != 0, append S mapped array into the mapped block (grow via 0x474e640 if needed, store new len at block+0x10); value = fresh S {first word, mapped block, static empty-map block}",
    "insert: copy head bytes into a fresh allocation (len 0 -> pointer 1), call 0x474b620(&S+0x20, key {len, ptr, len}, value); result dword 6 -> return; otherwise free the displaced array via the dealloc slot and drop the displaced sub-record at result+0x20 via 0x4742960"
  ],
  "verdict": "The insert helper treats S as the root of a \"::\"-keyed tree: it splits the element key on the first \"::\", probes the hash map embedded at S+0x20 (only when S+0x38 is nonzero) with an FNV-1a/0xff-terminated head hash, recurses into the matching bucket's child S with the tail, and otherwise inserts the head segment with a fresh child S as value -- built by recursing on the tail when S's map was empty, or, at a leaf, from the element's first word and the mapped nested block, appending S's own mapped array into that block first when the element's +0x38 low byte is nonzero. The helper body stores nothing to S directly; S changes only through the map insert at S+0x20 and through recursion into stored children."
}
